## Env vars the Go backend reads that compose.prod.yml does not deliver to the
## backend/worker containers, each with a decision. Read by scripts/check-compose-env.sh.
##
##   KEY | omit | reason    deliberately not delivered: the Go default is right for prod
##   KEY | wire | reason    should be delivered; reported as a warning until it is
##
## Any other read-but-undelivered key fails CI: wire it into compose.prod.yml's
## x-backend-environment block (KEY: ${KEY:-} keeps the Go default when unset),
## or record a decision here. Stale lines (key no longer read, or an `omit` key
## that is now delivered) fail too.

# Storage aliases and local driver: S3_* is canonical, MinIO stays private.
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY | omit | alias of S3_ACCESS_KEY
MINIO_BUCKET | omit | alias of S3_BUCKET
MINIO_ENDPOINT | omit | alias of S3_ENDPOINT
MINIO_PUBLIC_BASE_URL | omit | alias of S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL; browsers never get bucket URLs
MINIO_REGION | omit | alias of S3_REGION
MINIO_SECRET_KEY | omit | alias of S3_SECRET_KEY
MINIO_USE_PATH_STYLE | omit | alias of S3_USE_PATH_STYLE
S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL | omit | the bucket is private; media URLs are API-owned
STORAGE_LOCAL_PATH | omit | only for STORAGE_DRIVER=local, not used by the prod stack

# Fixed by the prod stack.
CENTRIFUGO_ENABLED | omit | Centrifugo is part of the prod stack (backend depends_on it)
REDIS_DB | omit | each app has its own Redis; DB 0
SMTP_FROM | omit | legacy alias of MAIL_FROM, which is delivered
